      "writtenOn": "2026-10-31T16:46:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two sources of truth for the QEMU 11 configure flags: qemu-build-policy.json lists --disable-download and omits --target-list, while compile-qemu.sh\u0027s live 26.04 path hardcodes a different flag set without --disable-download - and that\u0027s what CI actually builds with. validate_build() in qemu-artifact.py even requires --disable-download for ninja builds, so an artifact identity computed from the policy wouldn\u0027t match what compile-qemu.sh actually compiles. This is latent today since reuse isn\u0027t wired into the live pipeline, but once S3/S7 turns it on, reuse could substitute a binary built with different flags. Please unify the policy and compile-qemu.sh (ideally have compile-qemu.sh consume the policy), or explicitly document this as a known gap.",
      "tag": "review",
      "revId": "e0d798540a49ab5013a325a8d30d436e66022b11",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
